{{ macros.section(3, "Golang Polyglot", id="golang-polyglot") }}

`code.golang.cmk` lets you embed **inline Go** in a `compose.mk`/CMK program: it cross-builds[^xc] the
source in a dockerized Go toolchain, caches the resulting binary per-host, and execs it.  No Go
install is required on the host, and a clean (cache-hit) run just execs the cached binary.

```make
$(call include.plugins, code.golang.cmk)
```

{{ macros.section(3, "How it works", id="how-it-works") }}

The Go source is the **banana body** of a native `code.golang NAME(| body |)` construction; the
`go.mod` is **auto-generated** (a minimal module) unless you pass `mod=<block-ref>` for dependencies.
On first use the plugin:

1. cross-compiles for the host (`GOOS`/`GOARCH` auto-detected, env-overridable) inside the toolchain
   image, then chowns the output back to the host UID;
2. caches the binary under the `CMK_XDG_CACHE` directory at a `<hash>/<name>` path, keyed by a checksum of the **source + module**
   content: so editing either triggers a clean rebuild, and an unchanged program is a cache HIT;
3. execs it, forwarding any arguments.

{{ macros.section(3, "Public surface", id="public-surface") }}

| Symbol | Args | Purpose |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `code.golang NAME(| body |)` | `[mod=] ..` | native construction: wires a `NAME` (run) target and a `NAME/%` (run with the stem as argv) target |
| `code.golang.lambda` | `src= [mod=] [name=] [base=] [args=]` | build-if-needed, then exec |
| `code.golang.ensure` | `<src>,<mod>,<name>,<base>` | build-if-absent (a cache HIT just logs) |
| `code.golang.base` | -- | the toolchain image (default `golang:1.24-alpine`, overridable) |

